# Human gate for knowledge artifacts (dewey #194, epic #153 Phase 5).
#
# Under dewey #203, merging a code-owner-approved PR is the trust vouch that
# marks a knowledge page as validated, so compiled and curated knowledge
# requires human code-owner review before it can merge. A bot approval
# (e.g. uf-divisor) does not satisfy the code-owner requirement, so a PR
# touching these paths stays blocked until @jflowers approves.
#
# .uf/dewey/learnings/** is deliberately unowned: learnings are always draft
# tier and reach main through daily chore(dewey) PRs that must keep
# auto-merging. All other paths are likewise unowned, so regular code PRs
# pick up no new review requirement.
#
# This file only takes effect once "Require review from Code Owners" is
# enabled on the default-branch ruleset — an admin repo-settings edit, not
# code, and not committed here.
.uf/dewey/compiled/** @jflowers
.uf/dewey/knowledge/** @jflowers
